# Spendly ERD — Mermaid source

The ERD is split into bounded diagrams for readability. `||--o{` means one-to-many; `}o--o{` indicates many-to-many resolved by an associative entity.
The canonical inventory contains 30 entities, matching the logical schema and column contract.
UUID primary and foreign keys shown below use `BINARY(16)`; currency codes remain natural keys. Monetary amount fields use `DECIMAL(19,4)`. `FX_RATES.rate` is a conversion rate, not a monetary amount, and its precision is unspecified pending future FX design.
Reusable records use `ACTIVE`/`ARCHIVED`; budget periods use `OPEN`/`CLOSED`, with exact transition rules to be defined before API work. New accounts default out of Safe-to-Spend. Spaces take the owner's/household's chosen IANA timezone at creation; each period snapshots it, and historical period dates/timezones remain fixed. Personal spaces remain private; household spaces are visible to active members, while transactions require explicit sharing. Any allocation change clears mixed-allocation consent and resets sharing to `PRIVATE`. Invitations grant `MEMBER` only; ownership transfer is separate. Sound defaults off; reduced motion initializes from the platform preference and allows explicit override.

## 1. Identity, household and spaces

```mermaid
erDiagram
    USERS ||--o{ SESSIONS : authenticates
    USERS ||--|| USER_PREFERENCES : configures
    USERS ||--o{ HOUSEHOLD_MEMBERSHIPS : joins
    HOUSEHOLDS ||--o{ HOUSEHOLD_MEMBERSHIPS : contains
    HOUSEHOLDS ||--o{ HOUSEHOLD_INVITATIONS : invites
    USERS ||--o{ HOUSEHOLD_INVITATIONS : creates
    USERS ||--o{ SPACES : owns_personal
    HOUSEHOLDS ||--o{ SPACES : owns_shared

    USERS {
      uuid BINARY(16) id PK
      string email_normalized UK
      string password_hash
      string status
      string primary_currency_code FK
      string timezone
    }
    SESSIONS {
      uuid BINARY(16) id PK
      uuid BINARY(16) user_id FK
      string token_hash UK
      datetime expires_at
      datetime revoked_at
    }
    USER_PREFERENCES {
      uuid BINARY(16) user_id PK,FK
      string theme_key
      string communication_style
      string motion_level
      boolean sound_enabled
      boolean reduced_motion
      json notification_preferences
    }
    HOUSEHOLDS {
      uuid BINARY(16) id PK
      string name
      uuid BINARY(16) created_by_user_id FK
      string status
    }
    HOUSEHOLD_MEMBERSHIPS {
      uuid BINARY(16) id PK
      uuid BINARY(16) household_id FK
      uuid BINARY(16) user_id FK
      string role
      string status
    }
    HOUSEHOLD_INVITATIONS {
      uuid BINARY(16) id PK
      uuid BINARY(16) household_id FK
      uuid BINARY(16) created_by_user_id FK
      string token_hash UK
      string role_to_grant
      datetime expires_at
      datetime revoked_at
    }
    SPACES {
      uuid BINARY(16) id PK
      uuid BINARY(16) owner_user_id FK
      uuid BINARY(16) household_id FK
      string name
      string type
      string timezone
      string visibility_policy
    }
```

**Invariant:** `SPACES.owner_user_id` XOR `SPACES.household_id` — exactly one must be non-null.

## 2. Financial event, ledger and attribution

```mermaid
erDiagram
    CURRENCIES ||--o{ ACCOUNTS : denominates
    CURRENCIES ||--o{ FINANCIAL_TRANSACTIONS : denominates
    USERS ||--o{ ACCOUNTS : owns_personal
    HOUSEHOLDS ||--o{ ACCOUNTS : owns_shared
    ACCOUNTS ||--o{ ACCOUNT_ENTRIES : receives
    FINANCIAL_TRANSACTIONS ||--o{ ACCOUNT_ENTRIES : posts
    FINANCIAL_TRANSACTIONS ||--o{ TRANSACTION_ALLOCATIONS : attributes
    SPACES ||--o{ TRANSACTION_ALLOCATIONS : receives
    CATEGORIES ||--o{ TRANSACTION_ALLOCATIONS : classifies
    FINANCIAL_TRANSACTIONS ||--o| TRANSFER_DETAILS : describes_transfer
    ACCOUNT_ENTRIES ||--o| TRANSFER_DETAILS : source_entry
    ACCOUNT_ENTRIES ||--o| TRANSFER_DETAILS : destination_entry
    FINANCIAL_TRANSACTIONS ||--o| FINANCIAL_TRANSACTIONS : replaced_by

    CURRENCIES {
      string code PK
      string name
      string symbol
      int minor_unit_digits
    }
    ACCOUNTS {
      uuid BINARY(16) id PK
      uuid BINARY(16) owner_user_id FK
      uuid BINARY(16) household_id FK
      string name
      string type
      string currency_code FK
      boolean include_in_safe_to_spend
      string status
    }
    CATEGORIES {
      uuid BINARY(16) id PK
      uuid BINARY(16) owner_user_id FK
      uuid BINARY(16) household_id FK
      string name
      string kind
      boolean is_system_default
    }
    FINANCIAL_TRANSACTIONS {
      uuid BINARY(16) id PK
      uuid BINARY(16) created_by_user_id FK
      string transaction_type
      string status
      DECIMAL(19,4) amount
      string currency_code FK
      datetime occurred_at
      uuid BINARY(16) original_transaction_id FK
      uuid BINARY(16) replaces_transaction_id FK,UK
      string household_share_status
      datetime mixed_allocation_consent_at
    }
    ACCOUNT_ENTRIES {
      uuid BINARY(16) id PK
      uuid BINARY(16) transaction_id FK
      uuid BINARY(16) account_id FK
      DECIMAL(19,4) amount_signed
      string currency_code FK
      string entry_role
    }
    TRANSACTION_ALLOCATIONS {
      uuid BINARY(16) id PK
      uuid BINARY(16) transaction_id FK
      uuid BINARY(16) space_id FK
      uuid BINARY(16) category_id FK
      uuid BINARY(16) beneficiary_user_id FK
      DECIMAL(19,4) amount
      uuid BINARY(16) reverses_allocation_id FK
    }
    TRANSFER_DETAILS {
      uuid BINARY(16) transaction_id PK,FK
      uuid BINARY(16) source_account_entry_id FK,UK
      uuid BINARY(16) destination_account_entry_id FK,UK
    }
```

Posted transactions require their documented account entries; drafts may have none. Transfer details reference both source and destination entries through unique composite FKs paired with `transaction_id`, enforcing same-transaction ownership. `budget_allocations.category_id` is nullable; a generated normalized key enforces one flexible pool per period.

Correction and refund relationships are distinct: `replaces_transaction_id` on a replacement points to its voided predecessor and is unique, while `original_transaction_id` links a posted refund to its original expense. Original voided entries/allocations remain for audit and are excluded from current balances/reporting; correction creates no reversing entries. Composite candidate keys support currency consistency; see `DATABASE_COLUMN_CONTRACT.md`.

## 3. Income forecasts and receipts

```mermaid
erDiagram
    INCOME_SOURCES ||--o{ INCOME_SCHEDULES : defines
    INCOME_SOURCES ||--o{ INCOME_OCCURRENCES : originates
    INCOME_SCHEDULES ||--o{ INCOME_OCCURRENCES : forecasts
    SPACES ||--o{ INCOME_SCHEDULES : scopes
    SPACES ||--o{ INCOME_OCCURRENCES : scopes
    INCOME_OCCURRENCES ||--o{ INCOME_RECEIPTS : reconciles
    FINANCIAL_TRANSACTIONS ||--o| INCOME_RECEIPTS : reconciles_once

    INCOME_SOURCES {
      uuid BINARY(16) id PK
      uuid BINARY(16) owner_user_id FK
      string name
      string source_type
      string status
    }
    INCOME_SCHEDULES {
      uuid BINARY(16) id PK
      uuid BINARY(16) income_source_id FK
      uuid BINARY(16) space_id FK
      DECIMAL(19,4) expected_amount
      string currency_code
      string frequency_type
      string recurrence_rule
      date expected_next_date
    }
    INCOME_OCCURRENCES {
      uuid BINARY(16) id PK
      uuid BINARY(16) income_schedule_id FK
      uuid BINARY(16) income_source_id FK
      uuid BINARY(16) space_id FK
      DECIMAL(19,4) expected_amount
      string currency_code
      date expected_date
      string status
    }
    INCOME_RECEIPTS {
      uuid BINARY(16) id PK
      uuid BINARY(16) income_occurrence_id FK
      uuid BINARY(16) transaction_id FK
      DECIMAL(19,4) received_amount
      datetime received_at
    }
```

Expected occurrences do not create account entries. Actual receipt transactions do. An occurrence may have many partial receipt rows; each receipt links to one transaction and a transaction links to at most one occurrence (unique receipt transaction ID). Cumulative receipt overpayment is rejected until an adjustment policy is approved.

## 4. Budgets, commitments, goals and reserves

```mermaid
erDiagram
    SPACES ||--o{ BUDGET_PLANS : owns
    BUDGET_PLANS ||--o{ BUDGET_PERIODS : instantiates
    BUDGET_PERIODS ||--o{ BUDGET_ALLOCATIONS : plans
    CATEGORIES ||--o{ BUDGET_ALLOCATIONS : classifies
    SPACES ||--o{ COMMITMENT_TEMPLATES : owns
    COMMITMENT_TEMPLATES ||--o{ COMMITMENT_OCCURRENCES : generates
    SPACES ||--o{ COMMITMENT_OCCURRENCES : scopes
    COMMITMENT_OCCURRENCES ||--o{ COMMITMENT_PAYMENTS : paid_by
    FINANCIAL_TRANSACTIONS ||--o{ COMMITMENT_PAYMENTS : actual_payment
    SPACES ||--o{ GOALS : owns
    GOALS ||--o{ GOAL_CONTRIBUTIONS : tracks
    FUND_RESERVATIONS ||--o| GOAL_CONTRIBUTIONS : earmarked_by
    ACCOUNTS ||--o{ FUND_RESERVATIONS : reserves_from

    BUDGET_PLANS {
      uuid BINARY(16) id PK
      uuid BINARY(16) space_id FK
      string name
      string currency_code
      string period_type
      string status
    }
    BUDGET_PERIODS {
      uuid BINARY(16) id PK
      uuid BINARY(16) budget_plan_id FK
      date period_start
      date period_end
      string timezone_snapshot
      string status
    }
    BUDGET_ALLOCATIONS {
      uuid BINARY(16) id PK
      uuid BINARY(16) budget_period_id FK
      uuid BINARY(16) category_id FK
      uuid BINARY(16) category_unique_key generated
      DECIMAL(19,4) planned_amount
    }
    COMMITMENT_TEMPLATES {
      uuid BINARY(16) id PK
      uuid BINARY(16) space_id FK
      string name
      DECIMAL(19,4) expected_amount
      string currency_code
      string recurrence_rule
    }
    COMMITMENT_OCCURRENCES {
      uuid BINARY(16) id PK
